# OPAC sulfate-droplet complex refractive index, 0.25-40 um, at eight relative
# humidities.
#
# columns: mode  rh_percent  wavelength_um  n  k
#
# `suso` is OPAC's sulfate component: 75% sulphuric acid solution, the
# composition it uses for the Antarctic and stratospheric background aerosol.
# It is the right composition for VOLCANIC sulfate, which is emitted as SO2 and
# oxidised to sulphuric acid, and it is NOT OPAC's `waso` water-soluble
# component, which is an internal mixture including nitrate and organics and
# describes a continental anthropogenic aerosol this world does not have.
#
# Hess, Koepke & Schult (1998), doi 10.1175/1520-0477(1998)079<0831:OPOAAC>2.0.CO;2,
# obtained from libRadtran 2.0.6 data/aerosol/OPAC/refractive_indices/, the same
# route and release as the mineral and sea-salt tables beside it. k ships
# negative in OPAC and the sign is flipped here.
